he story unfold through  the lens of one who's not exactly a  fighter through foss's perspective we're  then given a show that heavily deals  with tragedy self-image and loss it's  more than an action show and it's an  anime that i can confidently introduce  to a non-fan at least compared to  something like yujosenki the 3d  presentation might discourage some  people from watching the show but it is  actually surprisingly well done if i  were to look at an action show as a  whole in terms of value and not just  popcorn entertainment land of the  lustrous easily takes the top spot this  year  2018  as we inch closer to the end of the  decade we start getting into the action  shows that made a buzz in the community  for good or bad reasons who could forget  goblin slayer's controversy or the  weekly reactions darling in the  frankstra of the community this year  also marked golden kamui's debut and  while its focus is more exploration and  adventure it's got some good action and  it's one of the shows that i just  couldn't get enough of slime also  started this year and it's poised to be  one of the big isekai hits in the coming  years as far as anime adaptations go if  we're talking straight action that can  see some mainstream appeal to non-fans i  think that few can top megalo box for  that year combining a lot of classic  western aesthetics with an epic boxing  setting made for a wondrous addition to  the library of action anime people have  called it an exciting anime that looked  like a heavy sci-fi cross between cowboy  bebop and samurai shamplo and it's easy  to see why it has its own unique style  from the presentation to the music and  has that nostalgic 90s feel that a lot  of people have grown to love but one of  the main reasons i'd recommend this  anime to someone is because how amazing  the second season which he had this year  was and don't get me wrong the first  season was good and all but the second  season for me is just on another tier  easily won the best anime of 2021 so far  so in a different twist megalo box is  actually something that i would  recommend more to older fans those who  went through the 90s and had taken a  break from anime it should bring back  memories of those good old days that  they'll surely enjoy reliving  2019  right so we all know what 2019's about  but first let me talk about the  honorable mentions first up i had a  great time watching dororo fireforce and  shield hero and i'd recommend those to  anime fans wise man's grandchild is also  a fun show to watch although it only  caters to a specific niche so i can't  easily recommend that one as much the  same can be said of ari furetha but this  one also had the dubious distinction of  possibly some of the worst cg in  animation i've seen in an anime for a  long time  ps1 monsters in 2019 anyone  we all know 2019 is the year of demon  slayer breaking into the mainstream like  nothing's ever done before heck i think  the demon slayer craze has officially  surpassed attack on titan with the manga  the opening song and even the recent  movie shattering records left and right  but  i give the nod this year  to vinland saga i just feel that as an  action series finland sanger just brings  so much more to the table than demon  slayer i can understand why the latter  became more popular but where vinland  saga lacked in the flashy explosive ufo  table animations and cool powers it  brought with a more grounded and  complete story the way i see it the  narrative gets developed better and the  characters are a tier above demon  slayer's characters in terms of writing  and characterization i'm not saying that  demons say characters are bad or bland  because that's not the case the finland  saga's cast just feels way better if  we're going to look at it from a  critical perspective a captivating story  of hardship and growth filled with epic  action of very complex characters  finland saga's my pick for 2019's action  anime  2020  we come to the end of the decade 2020  for me will always be the year of delays  due to the real world circumstances as  well as the year of sequels if we take  all the sequels movies and ovas out the  way you're actually left with a few gems  i had a blast with the trio of edgy  action titles dora hidaro darwin's game  and gleipnir the dragon quest anime was  also fun and the duo of princess connect  and both three are probably two of my  favorite chill action shows the past  year but things would change in this  rather slow year for non-sequels as it  marched towards the end with what i can  feel to be suspiciously demon slayer's  spiritual successor jujutsu kaizen  no the two shows aren't related but i  think the demon slayer's smashing  success had a bit to do with jiu jitsu  kaizen getting the green light i mean  there's also the revival of shaman king  and bleach not long after it's like that  time when many shows with the attack on  titan approach got green lit giving us  galvaneri of the iron fortress black  bullet seraph of the end and gordita  whatever the case though supernatural  actions shonen are back on the menu and  jiu jitsu kaizen is now leading the  charge like demon slayer jiu jitsu  kaizen is a show mostly carried by how  good it looks the action's good the  characters are relatable and likable and  the powers are interesting that's  basically the recipe you use to turn in  a winner in the realm of action shonen  and jiu-jitsu kaizen passes the test  with flying colours every other episode  gave us a moment or a reveal that set  the whole anime community ablaze with  discussions and i'd say that you've got  to give a lot of credit to the animation  team for that  2021  and here we are 2021 and we're still  reeling from the effects of 2020 on the  bright side the anime industry seemed to  have recovered and stabilized from the  shock of early 2020 and there have been  a lot less delays now 2021's still not  over so we can't know for sure whether  this will hold but as far as an action  anime go i'll give the title this year  to vv florida's song i didn't know what  to expect out of vv fluoride diet song  at first despite the fact that the guy  behind re zero was involved in it it's  an understatement to say that the show  just blew me away with its incredible  animation and an often underrated aspect  in action anime the music and it  packages everything in a very  well-placed action anime that has quite  the depth in terms of themes one that's  becoming more and more relevant to  society gets integrated with technology  despite vv winning the title for 2021's  best action anime the year has had a lot  of strong contenders vivi just felt to  be the most complete for widespread  appeal for lack of a better term the  violence isn't extreme the fan service  is little to non-existent and the story  is well paced and has a good conclusion  you have 86 for those who want tragedy  drama and military in their action  series 2021 also unleashed mushoku  tensei known as the granddaddy of isakai  for a lot to the world and by the looks  of it it seems that it will stay for  good we have a long ride ahead if you  prefer something that involves time  loops however why don't you try tokyo  revengers it has a gripping plot that  continues to keep me on the edge of my  seat  that was a long discussion i'll be glad  to talk about it more on the comments  section come on show you year by year  picks as well and we can compare our  list honestly it's been quite a while  since i've had this much fun writing a  video because i've got to look at the  anime world from a perspective and see  how it has evolved over time if you  enjoyed this video as much as i did make  sure to hit that like button and share  this video with as many friends as you  can then maybe we can branch off to  other genres in the future best comedies  best mystery there's so much we can do  with this and i'll need your response to  see if i should keep making this new 